comments.body:
Hello Rahul! since its not testing “network policies” feature but more so its testing the specific policies you are adding for your component and the traffic flow associated with that, I would propose that this belongs in the suite of your own component - in this case in config operator repo
every team in OCP is adding network policies to their components - this doesn’t mean those e2e tests land in origin/networking suite
it should land in each component’s e2e lanes IMHO

@danwinship where did you add E2Es for our components - was it done in CNO Itself?
@knobunc what's the recommendation here? (I don't think adding every components policy tests to networking suite is scalable - we can't own those and ensure they are not flaky etc)
